<LegalPage title="Trust &amp; security | GetMine.ai" description="How GetMine approaches security today, what we are building toward, and what we do not yet claim." canonical="https://getmine.ai/trust">
    <p class="page-eyebrow">Trust &amp; security</p>
    <h1 class="page-headline">Your vault stays with you.</h1>

    <aside class="policy-summary"><strong>The short version:</strong> your vault lives on your computer and we hold no copy. What leaves is decided by your question, relayed but never kept by us &mdash; and where security is still being built, this page says so plainly.</aside>

    <p class="page-lead">GetMine is built so your health information can work for you without giving up control. This page is how we approach security today, what we are building toward, and &mdash; just as important &mdash; <strong>what we do not yet claim</strong>.</p>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>Local-first by design</h2>
      <p>Your vault lives on your device. The day-to-day work of organising and recalling your information happens locally, on hardware you own. We hold no copy of your records, and nothing leaves your device on its own.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>Your question decides what is shared</h2>
      <p>When Mina answers, only the slice of your records that the question needs is sent to the AI provider &mdash; relayed through GetMine&rsquo;s server, which keeps none of the content. Never your whole vault, and never your logins. Nothing leaves at rest, and nothing leaves without a question that requires it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>You set the terms</h2>
      <p>Sharing happens by choice, per source and per permission, and what you have chosen is always visible in the app. You can disconnect a source or withdraw a consent whenever you choose, and doing so stops any further use immediately. An answer already given cannot be unsaid &mdash; so what changes is what happens next, which is the honest shape of any consent.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>The logins you grant</h2>
      <p>Credentials for the sources you connect are stored encrypted on your machine, with the key kept outside the vault folder. A copy of your vault folder, wherever it ends up, contains no usable login to anything.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>A verified installer</h2>
      <p>The installer is signed by GETMINE LTD &mdash; notarised by Apple, publisher-verified by Microsoft. Your computer checks that signature before anything installs.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>What we do not claim today</h2>
      <p>Being useful about security means being exact about its limits.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The vault folder is not encrypted by the app.</strong> It relies on your operating system&rsquo;s own disk encryption (FileVault on macOS, BitLocker on Windows) &mdash; which we recommend you switch on. Application-level encryption of the vault is future work, not a property we have today.</li>
        <li><strong>Your records are as safe as your computer.</strong> Keeping it protected, and being careful where you copy or share your vault folder, is in your hands, as it would be with paper records.</li>
        <li><strong>We hold no formal certifications.</strong> We have not sought SOC&nbsp;2 or ISO&nbsp;27001, and we do not make claims we cannot back up. We will pursue the right ones as the product and the team grow.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>A foundation, not a destination</h2>
      <p>We are a small team in open beta. Security is foundational and we treat it that way: as GetMine matures our posture will deepen &mdash; more controls, more transparency, and progressively more of the architecture running at the edge. We will keep publishing plain-English documentation as that happens, and we will say when something changes.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Write to <a href="mailto:privacy@getmine.ai">privacy@getmine.ai</a> for any trust or security question. We will answer honestly &mdash; and if our answer is &ldquo;not yet&rdquo;, we will say so.</p>
      <p>The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> is the governing statement; where the two could be read differently, the privacy policy prevails.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="page-lead" style="font-size:.85em;opacity:.75">GetMine Ltd &middot; Version 1.0 &middot; 29 July 2026</p>
</LegalPage>

